{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SparselyIndexedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"edgeIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" describe dense indices with no holes and keep"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their laws. A conformer reports them only while it has no holes of that kind."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Algorithms over the incidence rows use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with arrays while holes exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are upper bounds only. Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and nothing in the library allocates by it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexPosition(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atPosition:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are inverses, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is true exactly for the positions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":", all in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":", which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" lists in increasing order."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without holes, the bounds equal "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":", and positions are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_numberedIncidenceRows()"},{"type":"text","text":" numbers the live vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the live edges "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and lists, for each vertex number, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbers of the far ends of its edge ends with the edge numbers beside them, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order (a self-loop twice)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/sparselyindexedgraph"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SparselyIndexedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedGraph.swift#L25"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SparselyIndexedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SparselyIndexedGraph","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015SparselyIndexedA0P","symbolKind":"protocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SparselyIndexedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedGraph\/edgePositionBound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\